From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] main: stop the 2-second cloud status poll writing logs

The frontend calls emudeck("cloud_decky_check_status") every 2 s for as long
as Decky runs. Each call logged the full command line at INFO (into the
journal through the plugin loader) and rewrote ~/.config/EmuDeck/logs/decky.log
— about 43,000 of each a day, on flash. With EmuDeck's backend missing, as on
a fresh install, every one of them was also a failed python3 spawn.

Return early when backend/api.py does not exist (the caller got "" before as
well, from the failed run). When it does, the poll still runs but no longer
logs or rewrites decky.log; every other command logs as before.

---
--- a/main.py
+++ b/main.py
@@ -45,17 +45,29 @@
 
     async def emudeck(self, command):
 
+        # Without EmuDeck's backend there is nothing to run. The UI polls
+        # cloud_decky_check_status every 2 s regardless, so return before a
+        # subprocess, a log line and a decky.log rewrite on every poll.
+        if not (emudeck_backend / "api.py").exists():
+            return ""
+        poll = command == "cloud_decky_check_status"
+
         if os.name == 'nt':
             bash_command = f"python {emudeck_backend}/api.py {command}"
         else:
             bash_command = f"python3 {emudeck_backend}/api.py {command}"
 
-        log(bash_command)
+        if not poll:
+            log(bash_command)
 
         result = subprocess.run(bash_command, shell=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
 
         cleaned_stdout = result.stdout.strip()
 
+        # The status poll keeps decky.log as the last real command left it.
+        if poll:
+            return cleaned_stdout
+
         os.makedirs(emudeck_logs, exist_ok=True)
 
         # Escribir el resultado en un archivo de log
